message: "Please cite the relevant theorem paper and computational specification, and cite the underlying arithmetic sources separately."
type: software
title: "Polynomial presentations of the integers over the rationals"
authors:
  - name: "JUVa"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JoseBrox/diophantine-z-q_improvements"
url: "https://github.com/JoseBrox/diophantine-z-q_improvements"
date-released: 2026-11-09
version: "2026.11.09-v13"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Mathematical papers and exact computational specifications for polynomial
  presentations of the integers over the rationals under stated arithmetic
  hypotheses. The leading existence constructions have 27 variables with
  degree less than 2^151 and 279 variables with exact degree four, with
  ineffective sufficient coefficient thresholds. Fully specified constructions
  have 29 variables with degree less than 2^157 and 322 variables with exact
  degree four. The latter has coefficient height 80989^109858+1.
  Structural results include weighted finite-algebra elimination, degree and
  coordinate lower bounds, elliptic height estimates, optimal square
  predicates, number-field definability reductions, and local obstructions
  to specified constructions. Every variable count includes the input.
keywords:
  - Diophantine definitions
  - Hilbert's tenth problem
  - rational points
  - explicit polynomials
  - elliptic heights
  - finite algebraic elimination
  - number fields
